i    Philosophy	fake	(NULL)	0
i    ----------	fake	(NULL)	0
i  Markdown is intended to be as easy-to-read and easy-to-write as  	fake	(NULL)	0
iis feasible.                                                       	fake	(NULL)	0
i	fake	(NULL)	0
i  Readability, however, is emphasized above all else. A            	fake	(NULL)	0
iMarkdown-formatted document should be publishable as-is, as plain  	fake	(NULL)	0
itext, without looking like it's been marked up with tags or        	fake	(NULL)	0
iformatting instructions. While Markdown's syntax has been          	fake	(NULL)	0
iinfluenced by several existing text-to-HTML filters -- including   	fake	(NULL)	0
iSetext, atx, Textile, reStructuredText, Grutatext, and EtText --   	fake	(NULL)	0
ithe single biggest source of inspiration for Markdown's syntax is  	fake	(NULL)	0
ithe format of plain text email.                                    	fake	(NULL)	0
i	fake	(NULL)	0
h"Setext"	URL:http://docutils.sourceforge.net/mirror/setext.html	localhost	70
h"atx"	URL:http://www.aaronsw.com/2002/atx/	localhost	70
h"Textile"	URL:http://textism.com/tools/textile/	localhost	70
h"reStructuredText"	URL:http://docutils.sourceforge.net/rst.html	localhost	70
h"Grutatext"	URL:http://www.triptico.com/software/grutatxt.html	localhost	70
