i    --------------	fake	(NULL)	0
i    Paragraphs and Line Breaks	fake	(NULL)	0
i    --------------------------	fake	(NULL)	0
i  A paragraph is simply one or more consecutive lines of text,     	fake	(NULL)	0
iseparated by one or more blank lines. (A blank line is any line    	fake	(NULL)	0
ithat looks like a blank line -- a line containing nothing but      	fake	(NULL)	0
ispaces or tabs is considered blank.) Normal paragraphs should not  	fake	(NULL)	0
ibe indented with spaces or tabs.                                   	fake	(NULL)	0
i	fake	(NULL)	0
i  The implication of the "one or more consecutive lines of text"   	fake	(NULL)	0
irule is that Markdown supports "hard-wrapped" text paragraphs.     	fake	(NULL)	0
iThis differs significantly from most other text-to-HTML formatters 	fake	(NULL)	0
i(including Movable Type's "Convert Line Breaks" option) which      	fake	(NULL)	0
itranslate every line break character in a paragraph into a `<br    	fake	(NULL)	0
i/>` tag.                                                           	fake	(NULL)	0
i	fake	(NULL)	0
i  When you do want to insert a `<br />` break tag using Markdown,  	fake	(NULL)	0
iyou end a line with two or more spaces, then type return.          	fake	(NULL)	0
i	fake	(NULL)	0
i    Headers	fake	(NULL)	0
i    -------	fake	(NULL)	0
i  Markdown supports two styles of headers, [Setext] [1] and [atx]  	fake	(NULL)	0
i[2].                                                               	fake	(NULL)	0
i	fake	(NULL)	0
i  Optionally, you may "close" atx-style headers. This is purely    	fake	(NULL)	0
icosmetic -- you can use this if you think it looks better. The     	fake	(NULL)	0
iclosing hashes don't even need to match the number of hashes used  	fake	(NULL)	0
ito open the header. (The number of opening hashes determines the   	fake	(NULL)	0
iheader level.)                                                     	fake	(NULL)	0
i	fake	(NULL)	0
i    Blockquotes	fake	(NULL)	0
i    -----------	fake	(NULL)	0
i  Markdown uses email-style `>` characters for blockquoting. If    	fake	(NULL)	0
iyou're familiar with quoting passages of text in an email message, 	fake	(NULL)	0
ithen you know how to create a blockquote in Markdown. It looks     	fake	(NULL)	0
ibest if you hard wrap the text and put a `>` before every line:    	fake	(NULL)	0
i	fake	(NULL)	0
i     |    This is a blockquote with two paragraphs. Lorem ipsum    	fake	(NULL)	0
i     |  dolor sit amet, consectetuer adipiscing elit. Aliquam      	fake	(NULL)	0
i     |  hendrerit mi posuere lectus. Vestibulum enim wisi,         	fake	(NULL)	0
i     |  viverra nec, fringilla in, laoreet vitae, risus.           	fake	(NULL)	0
i     |                                                             	fake	(NULL)	0
i     |    Donec sit amet nisl. Aliquam semper ipsum sit amet       	fake	(NULL)	0
i     |  velit. Suspendisse id sem consectetuer libero luctus       	fake	(NULL)	0
i     |  adipiscing.                                                	fake	(NULL)	0
i     |                                                             	fake	(NULL)	0
i                                                                   	fake	(NULL)	0
i  Markdown allows you to be lazy and only put the `>` before the   	fake	(NULL)	0
ifirst line of a hard-wrapped paragraph:                            	fake	(NULL)	0
i	fake	(NULL)	0
i     |    This is a blockquote with two paragraphs. Lorem ipsum    	fake	(NULL)	0
i     |  dolor sit amet, consectetuer adipiscing elit. Aliquam      	fake	(NULL)	0
i     |  hendrerit mi posuere lectus. Vestibulum enim wisi,         	fake	(NULL)	0
i     |  viverra nec, fringilla in, laoreet vitae, risus.           	fake	(NULL)	0
i     |                                                             	fake	(NULL)	0
i                                                                   	fake	(NULL)	0
i     |    Donec sit amet nisl. Aliquam semper ipsum sit amet       	fake	(NULL)	0
i     |  velit. Suspendisse id sem consectetuer libero luctus       	fake	(NULL)	0
i     |  adipiscing.                                                	fake	(NULL)	0
i     |                                                             	fake	(NULL)	0
i                                                                   	fake	(NULL)	0
