i    -----	fake	(NULL)	0
i  Markdown supports ordered (numbered) and unordered (bulleted)    	fake	(NULL)	0
ilists.                                                             	fake	(NULL)	0
i	fake	(NULL)	0
i  Unordered lists use asterisks, pluses, and hyphens --            	fake	(NULL)	0
iinterchangably -- as list markers:                                 	fake	(NULL)	0
i	fake	(NULL)	0
i      - Red                                                        	fake	(NULL)	0
i      - Green                                                      	fake	(NULL)	0
i      - Blue                                                       	fake	(NULL)	0
i                                                                   	fake	(NULL)	0
iis equivalent to:                                                  	fake	(NULL)	0
i	fake	(NULL)	0
i      - Red                                                        	fake	(NULL)	0
i      - Green                                                      	fake	(NULL)	0
i      - Blue                                                       	fake	(NULL)	0
i                                                                   	fake	(NULL)	0
iand:                                                               	fake	(NULL)	0
i	fake	(NULL)	0
i      - Red                                                        	fake	(NULL)	0
i      - Green                                                      	fake	(NULL)	0
i      - Blue                                                       	fake	(NULL)	0
i                                                                   	fake	(NULL)	0
iOrdered lists use numbers followed by periods:                     	fake	(NULL)	0
i	fake	(NULL)	0
i     1. Bird                                                       	fake	(NULL)	0
i     2. McHale                                                     	fake	(NULL)	0
i     3. Parish                                                     	fake	(NULL)	0
i                                                                   	fake	(NULL)	0
i  It's important to note that the actual numbers you use to mark   	fake	(NULL)	0
ithe list have no effect on the HTML output Markdown produces. The  	fake	(NULL)	0
iHTML Markdown produces from the above list is:                     	fake	(NULL)	0
i	fake	(NULL)	0
iIf you instead wrote the list in Markdown like this:               	fake	(NULL)	0
i	fake	(NULL)	0
i     1. Bird                                                       	fake	(NULL)	0
i     2. McHale                                                     	fake	(NULL)	0
i     3. Parish                                                     	fake	(NULL)	0
i                                                                   	fake	(NULL)	0
ior even:                                                           	fake	(NULL)	0
i	fake	(NULL)	0
i     3. Bird                                                       	fake	(NULL)	0
i     4. McHale                                                     	fake	(NULL)	0
i     5. Parish                                                     	fake	(NULL)	0
i                                                                   	fake	(NULL)	0
i  you'd get the exact same HTML output. The point is, if you want  	fake	(NULL)	0
ito, you can use ordinal numbers in your ordered Markdown lists, so 	fake	(NULL)	0
ithat the numbers in your source match the numbers in your          	fake	(NULL)	0
ipublished HTML. But if you want to be lazy, you don't have to.     	fake	(NULL)	0
i	fake	(NULL)	0
