i    Code Blocks	fake	(NULL)	0
i    -----------	fake	(NULL)	0
i  Pre-formatted code blocks are used for writing about programming 	fake	(NULL)	0
ior markup source code. Rather than forming normal paragraphs, the  	fake	(NULL)	0
ilines of a code block are interpreted literally. Markdown wraps a  	fake	(NULL)	0
icode block in both `<pre>` and `<code>` tags.                      	fake	(NULL)	0
i	fake	(NULL)	0
i  To produce a code block in Markdown, simply indent every line of 	fake	(NULL)	0
ithe block by at least 4 spaces or 1 tab.                           	fake	(NULL)	0
i	fake	(NULL)	0
iThis is a normal paragraph:                                        	fake	(NULL)	0
i	fake	(NULL)	0
i    +----------------------------------------------------------+   	fake	(NULL)	0
i    | This is a code block.                                    |   	fake	(NULL)	0
i    +----------------------------------------------------------+   	fake	(NULL)	0
i                                                                   	fake	(NULL)	0
