iindented (or the end of the article).                              	fake	(NULL)	0
i	fake	(NULL)	0
i  Within a code block, ampersands (`&`) and angle brackets (`<`    	fake	(NULL)	0
iand `>`) are automatically converted into HTML entities. This      	fake	(NULL)	0
imakes it very easy to include example HTML source code using       	fake	(NULL)	0
iMarkdown -- just paste it and indent it, and Markdown will handle  	fake	(NULL)	0
ithe hassle of encoding the ampersands and angle brackets. For      	fake	(NULL)	0
iexample, this:                                                     	fake	(NULL)	0
i	fake	(NULL)	0
